title: $:/plugins/nikorion/kms-ontology/language/en-GB/

Field/project/Label: Project
Field/project/Description: The project the tiddler belongs to: its organisational home.
Field/epistemology/Label: Epistemology
Field/epistemology/Description: How the knowledge in the tiddler is produced and validated: its methodological family (philosophy, formal sciences, human and social sciences, interpretive knowledge…).
Field/disciplines/Label: Disciplines
Field/disciplines/Description: The field(s) of study the tiddler belongs to (hermeneutics, sociology, biology…).
Field/technology/Label: Technology mobilised
Field/technology/Description: The technologies the tiddler mobilises: software, languages, platforms, techniques (TiddlyWiki, Node.js…).
Field/equipment/Label: Equipment mobilised
Field/equipment/Description: The physical equipment it mobilises: devices, instruments, tools (laptop, soldering iron…).
Field/role/Label: Role
Field/role/Description: What the tiddler is for: its function in the wiki — a way in, knowledge, a procedure, something to reuse, a register, tracking, a project or a tool.
Field/maturity/Label: Maturity
Field/maturity/Description: How far along the writing is.
Field/maturity/Applies: every role but registers and tasks
Field/lifecycle/Label: Lifecycle
Field/lifecycle/Description: Whether the tiddler is still in circulation. Independent of maturity: a stable tiddler can become obsolete.
Field/needs/Label: Needs
Field/needs/Description: The work the tiddler is waiting on.
Field/needs/Applies: every role but registers and tasks
Field/status/Label: Status
Field/status/Description: How far along a piece of work is.
Field/status/Applies: tasks, task lists and routines, or no role
